      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The well-known congenital anomalies of the left main stem refer mainly to its anomalous origin from the pulmonary artery or the right aortic sinus. We present a patient with a large communication between the left main stem trunk and the proximal segment of the left anterior descending coronary artery which preserves the left ventricular systolic performance in the setting of significant three-vessel disease."},
